The '''1966 NFL draft''' was held at the [[569 Lexington Avenue|Summit Hotel]] in [[New York City]] on Saturday, November 27, 1965.<ref name=HOF1966>{{cite web |url=http://www.profootballhof.com/history/story.jsp?story_id=1998|title=1966 NFL Draft|access-date=September 27, 2008 |publisher=Pro Football Hall of Fame}}</ref><ref name=taptal>{{cite news |url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=NLtOAAAAIBAJ&sjid=XQEEAAAAIBAJ&pg=7229%2C4865273 |newspaper=Toledo Blade |location=Ohio |agency=Associated Press |title=Nobis, Grabowski top picks as pros tap college talent|date=November 28, 1965 |page=3E }}</ref>

The expansion [[1966 Atlanta Falcons season|Atlanta Falcons]] were awarded the first pick in each round as well as the final pick in each of the first five rounds.<ref name=HOF1966/>  The [[List of first overall National Football League Draft picks|first overall selection]] was [[Tommy Nobis]], a [[linebacker]] from [[1965 Texas Longhorns football team|Texas]].<ref name=taptal/> The league also provided the Falcons with an [[1966 NFL expansion draft|expansion draft]] six weeks later.<ref name=HOF1966/>

This was the last draft in which the NFL and the [[American Football League|AFL]] selected their players separate of one another. As a result, most players drafted  by teams from both leagues chose to play for the more established NFL, but not all. Similar to [[1965 NFL draft|1965]], the [[1966 American Football League draft|AFL draft]] was held on the same day. After the [[AFL–NFL merger|merger agreement]] in June 1966, a common draft was held in March [[1967 NFL draft|1967]].

